\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces The representation and the dichotomy. \emph  {Top:} interaction lumps into one residual $d_{\rm  eff}$ on a fixed double integrator $\ddot  e = a_e + d_{\rm  eff}$. \emph  {Bottom:} the same-signed error demands \textbf  {opposite-sign} responses---capture \emph  {toward} the motion ($+\dot  e$) for a transient, integral hold \emph  {against} it for a sustained force. The discriminator is $d_{\rm  eff}$'s \emph  {persistence}, not its sign. The lower panels are conceptual illustrations, not measured responses.}}{4}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dichotomy}{{2}{4}{}{figure.2}{}}
